{"type": "message", "id": "dd90c9c5", "parentId": "86aba1b9", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T05:56:03.458Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_6bcc8e89b1494d8bb929f00c", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"railway suicides\\\" Germany 2014 2020 number statistics Eurostat data\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 857,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83f66d3e499e8e20\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBehavioral and location‐related antecedents of train suicides - Moritz - 2023 - Suicide and Life-Threatening Behavior - Wiley Online Library\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83f66d3e499e8e20\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/sltb.12941\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"817379ac569f535e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA psychiatric diagnosis, especially the presence of depression, was higher in the group of ITS than in the general population (27.8%; Jacobi et al., 2014, 2016), which is in accordance with studies that link risk of suicide with the presence of psychiatric illness (Bertolote et al., 2004; Haltenhof et al., 2013; Hansen et al., 2003; Sher, 2006). A total of 78.6% (n = 44) of the present sample were German nationals, which is somewhat lower than the proportion of individuals with German citizenship in Hamburg in 2020 (82.9%; Federal Statistical Office/Statistisches Bundesamt, 2021).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"817379ac569f535e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"onlinelibrary.wiley.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d350e196ccaa259b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nStable time patterns of railway suicides in Germany: comparative analysis of 7,187 cases across two observation periods (1995–1998; 2005–2008) - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d350e196ccaa259b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3933256/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc566b7685dda5a0\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe majority of fatalities on the European Union (EU) railways are suicides, representing <strong>about 60% of all railway fatalities</strong>. The aim of this study was to compare time patterns of suicidal behaviour on railway tracks in Germany between two ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc566b7685dda5a0\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fc28e790c7e4438\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTen-year incidence and time trends of railway suicides in Germany from 1991 to 2000 | European Journal of Public Health | Oxford Academic\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2fc28e790c7e4438\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://academic.oup.com/eurpub/article/16/2/173/505730\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"449c42af1a6a88ce\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMethods: From 1991 to 2000, a total of <strong>8653 fatal railway suicides</strong> were recorded by the national central registry of all passenger accidents on the German railway net. To assess time trends, the average annual percentage change (AAPC) of the ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"449c42af1a6a88ce\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 1, 2006\",\n      \"siteName\": \"academic.oup.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bbdb9a95a0ce1d59\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAbsolute numbers and rates (per 100 000 inhabitants) of railway... | Download Table\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bbdb9a95a0ce1d59\\\">>>\",\n     